{"_id":"68a736428ec3d8323af20408","nodeId":"cjAwawhZLo1qVQ93XIdm2","roadmapSlug":"typescript","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:45.916Z","description":"# Null Type in TypeScript\n\nThe `null` type represents the intentional absence of a value. It's a primitive data type that has only one possible value: `null`. It signifies that a variable or property has no value assigned to it, or that a value has been explicitly removed.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"null and undefined","url":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/everyday-types.html#null-and-undefined","_id":"69a965b0ff2299735324397d"}],"updatedAt":"2026-03-05T11:14:56.641Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d041649f","title":"Scrimba - Learn TypeScript","partner":"Scrimba","type":"course","url":"https://v2.scrimba.com/learn-typescript-c03c?via=roadmap"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/typescript/content/cjAwawhZLo1qVQ93XIdm2.md"}